        "geology": "The glacial basin is carved in the Oceanic Units of the Western and Ligurian Alps, in particular in the Gastaldi Greenstones Zone. Calcschists and Metabasites are the prevailing lithotypes. Calcschists are found mainly in the eastern part of the study area, while Metabasites form the “Uja di Bessanese” ridge. In the southern part of the basin, an isolated outcrop of Serpentinites is found.",
